    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Ottoman Empire grew from a frontier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#beylik">beylik</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#anatolia">Anatolia</a> into a power spanning three continents for over six centuries.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#janissaries">Janissary</a> infantry, gunpowder artillery and a sophisticated bureaucracy let it take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#constantinople">Constantinople</a> and rule a diverse realm.</li><li>Lost wars, nationalist revolts and European debt control eroded it; defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#first-world-war">First World War</a> ended the sultanate in 1922.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mimar-sinan">Mimar Sinan</a> is credited with more than three hundred buildings, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#suleymaniye-mosque">Süleymaniye Mosque</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#istanbul">Istanbul</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#selimiye-mosque">Selimiye Mosque</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#edirne">Edirne</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

